  {
    "attribution_required": true,
    "claim_id": "oil-import-comparisons",
    "claim_kind": "NUMBER",
    "claim_text": "The retained EIA summary also reports crude imports falling by 791,000 barrels a day to 6.0 million barrels a day. Its four-week import average was 6.1 million barrels a day, 0.9% above the year-earlier level. A weekly flow change, a four-week comparison and a stock change answer different questions; they do not supply a complete explanation of the crude draw.",
    "document_id": "goal27-oil-original",
    "source_id": "SOURCE_2",
    "support_excerpt_sha256": "51fc3c9242fa1f3a68e2bff376d20a865ae4abcafdf9fe4f54458930457e4dc6",
    "support_status": "SUPPORTED_EXACT_RETRIEVED_SOURCE_BYTES"
  },
  {
    "attribution_required": true,
    "claim_id": "oil-lower-buffer-countercase",
    "claim_kind": "FACT",
    "claim_text": "The countercase to dismissing the draw is that EIA places crude and distillate stocks below their five-year averages. Lower buffers could matter for availability even if stronger end demand has not been shown; persistence is the missing test.",
    "document_id": "goal27-oil-original",
    "source_id": "SOURCE_2",
    "support_excerpt_sha256": "e9ec4abbafbe8fe2e4356e03f0f0ce0cb05d446872abfb3a26889aaa46c2966b",
    "support_status": "SUPPORTED_EXACT_RETRIEVED_SOURCE_BYTES"
  },
  {
    "article_section_ids": [
      "paragraph:9"
    ],
    "attribution_required": true,
    "claim_id": "oil-market-evidence-limits",
    "claim_kind": "FACT",
    "claim_text": "A seasonal stock comparison is also different from a market surprise. Capital Chronicle has no separately captured pre-release expectation, contemporaneous WTI price response or current futures curve in this record. It therefore cannot establish what traders anticipated, how prices responded or whether that response reflected the inventory figures.",
